DESCRIPTION:\n\n\nFree! Dance instruction with music! Good exercise! All a
 re welcome! “A Festival of Bon-odori Dance and Japanese Street Food” Pres
 ented by the Japanese Language Circle\, Department of World Languages and
  Cultures\, and the Japan Club \n \nDate: Wednesday September 9th\, 2026 
 Time: 2:00-3:30 pm Place: The Underground\, Student Center room 160 Stree
 t Food: Takoyaki\, Yakisoba & Onigiri\, all homemade\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n
 \n\n\n\nThe Japanese Language Circle also known as J-Circle\, meets every
  Wednesday from 1:45 to 3:15 pm in Schmitt Hall room 125. This is a place
  where you make friends\, bring friends\, share your interest in Japanese
  Language and culture\, enjoy Japanese cuisine\, learn more Japanese. Bri
 ng friends! Next J-Circle event: 10/7 JET PROGRAM INFORMATION SESSION\, i
 n Schmitt Room 125\, by MSU alumni & The JET Program\, Consulate General 
 of Japan in New York. Spread the news!\n\n\n\n\nHosted by: College of Hum
 anities and Social Sciences (CHSS)\n\nAdditional Information can be found
  at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12677256
