BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:Social
CATEGORIES:Academic/Educational/Intellectual
DESCRIPTION:As part of Campus Fire Safety Awareness Month this September\,
  we are planning a large-scale educational event focused on raising aware
 ness about fire safety within the campus community. The highlight of the 
 event will be a live burn demonstration using the National Fire Sprinkler
  Association's (NFSA) Side-by-Side Trailer. This will feature two mock do
 rm rooms—one with a sprinkler system and one without—to showcase the dram
 atic impact fire safety systems can have during a fire.The goal of the ev
 ent is to educate students about the importance of working smoke detector
 s\, not blocking or tampering with sprinkler heads\, and understanding th
 at while sprinkler systems may cause water damage\, they ultimately save 
 lives.\n\nHosted by: Campus Activities\, Fire Safety\n\nAdditional Inform
 ation can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/1269
 3308
DTEND:20260911T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041743Z
DTSTART:20260910T230000Z
LOCATION:Student Center Quad/Student Center Ballrooms
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Flames & Facts
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12693308
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12693308
X-HOSTS:Fire Safety
END:VEVENT
