CATEGORIES:Service
CATEGORIES:Large Scale
DESCRIPTION:The 9/11 National Day of Service and Remembrance is long stand
 ing tradition at Montclair State University that honors the lives lost an
 d heroic acts of September 11\, 2001. Our volunteers commemorate the day 
 through meaningful service projects that foster unity\, civic responsibil
 ity\, leadership\, and often inspire long-term community engagement.\nCom
 e join us for a day of giving back!\nVolunteers will have the opportunity
  to choose from 20+ service sites\, both on and off campus\, and engage i
 n community service projects such as:\n\n🍎 Meal distribution and food pa
 ntry support\n🌳 Park and neighborhood cleanups\n🎨 Community revitalizat
 ion\n✨ Activities for youth\, seniors\, and adults with disabilities\n🧼 
 Assembling hygiene and snack kits\n And much more!\n\nHere’s what you can
  expect:\n\n⏰ Registration at 8:00 - 8:30 AM. Event starts at 8:30 AM\n🚌
  Transportation provided to and from off-campus sites\n🥯 Free breakfast 
 and lunch to fuel your day\n⏳ Service hours validation (for students/grou
 ps that need it)\n👕 Exclusive 9/11 Day of Service T-Shirt\n🧑‍🎓 Bloomfi
 eld College students will have a shuttle service provided\n🎊 Icebreaker 
 activities and giveaways!\n\n \nIMPORTANT NOTE: You can only sign up for 
 one service site due to each project running simultaneously. We will emai
 l you after registration if other information is needed for your site.\nS
 ign up link: https://www.eventzilla.net/e/911-national-day-of-service-and
 -remembrance-2026-2138674558\n\nHosted by: Office of Community Engagement
  and Partnerships\, Volunteer Center\n\nAdditional Information can be fou
 nd at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12552608
DTEND:20260912T180000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041743Z
DTSTART:20260912T120000Z
