DESCRIPTION:The Chinese Musicians Association of North America presents Th
 e Sound of Harvest\, a concert bringing together musicians and instrument
 s from a variety of cultural traditions. The program features Chinese ins
 truments such as the erhu\, pipa\, guzheng\, and ruan\, alongside Japanes
 e taiko and shinobue\, African percussion\, jazz piano\, lute\, guitar\, 
 cello\, double bass\, voice\, and more. \n \nThe Montclair performance wi
 ll take place on Sunday\, September 13\, 2026\, at 3:00 p.m. in Memorial 
 Auditorium at Montclair State University. The event is co-sponsored by th
 e Department of Global Cultural Studies.\n \nGet a glimpse of the concert
  and featured musical instruments here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r
 EIh15TquAY\n \nVisit ZEFFY to purchase ticketsStudent Promo Code:  MSU15 
  ($15 off the general admission price)\n \nView the official flyer for th
 is event here.\n\nHosted by: College of Humanities and Social Sciences (C
 HSS)\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://montclair.campusl
 abs.com/engage/event/12679147
