CATEGORIES:Civics
DESCRIPTION:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nJoin thousands of colleges\, universit
 ies\, nonprofits\, businesses\, and community organizations across the co
 untry as we celebrate National Voter Registration Day—the nation's larges
 t single-day voter registration effort. This annual\, nonpartisan initiat
 ive brings Americans together with one shared goal: helping eligible vote
 rs get registered\, informed\, and prepared to participate in our democra
 cy.\nJoin us on September 17 from 12:00–4:00 PM in the Student Center Bal
 lrooms and on the Quad as Montclair State University celebrates this nati
 onal movement with an afternoon of civic engagement\, entertainment\, and
  community.\nThis year's event is proudly presented in collaboration with
  the Office of Commuter Life as part of Commuter Life Appreciation Week (
 CLAW). Together\, we're celebrating the important role commuter students 
 play in our campus community while encouraging every Red Hawk to become a
 n informed and engaged participant in our democracy.\nWhether you're regi
 stering to vote for the first time\, updating your voter registration\, o
 r learning more about the upcoming election\, Race to the Ballot is your 
 one-stop destination to get election ready.\nThe event will kick off with
  welcoming remarks from Montclair State University President Dr. Jonathan
  Koppell\, who will officially open the celebration by speaking about the
  importance of civic participation and the power of student voices. Throu
 ghout the afternoon\, you'll also hear from special guest speakers who wi
 ll share their perspectives on the importance of voting\, civic leadershi
 p\, and making a difference in our communities.\nEnjoy a fun-filled after
 noon featuring:\n\nA giant patriotic inflatable obstacle course\nYard gam
 es and interactive activities\nFree food served throughout the event\nMus
 ic\, giveaways\, and civic swag\nVoter registration assistance and nonpar
 tisan election resources\nInteractive activities hosted by campus and com
 munity partners\n\nBe sure to stay for the entire event! Students who rem
 ain through the closing program will be entered into a raffle for a chanc
 e to win an exciting grand prize.\nTogether\, we're joining a nationwide 
 effort that has helped millions of Americans prepare to vote. Race to the
  Ballot is more than a voter registration event—it's a celebration of civ
 ic participation\, community\, and the belief that every voice has the po
 wer to shape the future.\nThe race starts here. The finish line is the ba
 llot box. Register\, get informed\, and join the movement!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\nHosted by: Campus Activities\, Civic & Voter Engagement\, Of
 fice of Commuter Life\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://
 montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12539370
DTEND:20260915T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041743Z
DTSTART:20260915T160000Z
LOCATION:Student Center Ballrooms and Quad
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:(Montclair Campus) National Voter Registration Day: Race to the Ba
 llot
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12539370
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12539370
X-HOSTS:Office of Commuter Life
