DESCRIPTION:Learn about the early history of Montclair State University on
  a 45-minute walking tour of the south end of campus. The tour will inclu
 de historic photographs of the oldest campus buildings and examples of me
 morabilia. We will discuss student life and interactions with the surroun
 ding Montclair community. Archivist\, Paul Martinez\, will lead the tour.
  We will meet in front of the Kasser Theater at 4 pm. Weather permitting 
 – the tour will be rescheduled in the event of rain. The tour is approxim
 ately half a mile long. Most of the route is accessible. There is an appr
 oximately 260-foot section which is partially-accessible due to a steep g
 rade.'\nRegister Here: https://montclair.libcal.com/event/17593469\n\nHos
 ted by: Sprague Library\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https:
 //montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12706559
