DESCRIPTION:LUPE Fund\, Inc's  "Power of Latinas: Strengthening Our Legacy
 \," conference and networking reception will be held at Montclair State U
 niversity's Hall Conference Center on October 1st\, 2026. LUPE Fund\, Inc
 .\, New Jersey's oldest Latina-run organization\, proudly celebrated its 
 20th anniversary in 2023. \nThe Conference Center is located at Montclair
  State University Campus\, at University Hall on the 7th Floor. \nJoin us
  for an inspiring and empowering event featuring panels in health & welln
 ess\, business\, politics\, and education. Each panelist is a powerful an
 d influential Latina dedicated to making a difference. Followed by a netw
 orking session\, don’t miss your chance to connect with these dynamic wom
 en and gain insights that could transform your personal and professional 
 life! Refreshments will be available. \nEvent Schedule\n2:00 PM - Registr
 ation Opens3:00 PM - Opening Remarks3:15 PM - Welcome Address3:30 PM - Ke
 ynote Speaker - Adel Wilson\, Assistant Secretary of State4:00 PM - Panel
  1 — Elección Latina: From Cultural Visibility to Civic Power5:10 PM - Di
 nner Break5:30 PM - Panel 2 — The Leadership Pipeline: Preparing Latinas 
 to Lead the Next Economy6:50 PM - Panel 3 — From Culture to Capital: Buil
 ding Latina Economic Power8:00 PM - Program Ends\nWe welcome all students
  to participate! Whether you're able to join us for the full event or jus
 t a portion\, this conference will offer valuable opportunities to engage
 .\n\nHosted by: Civic & Voter Engagement\, Government Relations and Commu
 nity Affairs \, Office for Hispanic Initiatives\n\nAdditional Information
  can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12540419
DTEND:20261002T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041743Z
DTSTART:20261001T180000Z
LOCATION:University Hall Conference Center
